# Documentation

Kinsenas uses **plain markdown in the main repo** — no Docusaurus sites, no nested doc repos, no published URLs yet.

When the user asks to create or update documentation, route by audience.

## Where to put markdown

| Audience | Path | Primary reader |
|----------|------|----------------|
| Admin / operators | `docs/admin/<kebab-case>.md` | Staff using the **Inertia/React admin UI** |
| Members / end users | `docs/members/<kebab-case>.md` | App members (when needed) |
| Index / setup | `docs/README.md` | Anyone cloning or browsing docs locally |

Most guides are **admin-heavy**. Default to `docs/admin/` unless the content is clearly member-facing.

Use **kebab-case** filenames. Cross-link siblings with relative paths: `[Title](./sibling-page.md)`.

## Audience

- **Mixed content** → split into `docs/admin/` and `docs/members/` files; never one doc for both audiences
- **Technical** (APIs, algorithms, internal systems) → admin unless explicitly member-facing
- **Engineering-only** (migrations, artisan, deploy, SSH, test commands) → `.cursor/breakdowns/` only — not `docs/`

## Admin docs (`docs/admin/`)

Admin guides are for **operators using the Inertia admin UI** — not engineers on the server.

**Do not include in admin markdown:**

- `php artisan …` commands, shell blocks, or deploy/SSH instructions
- References to `.cursor/` paths (breakdowns, plans, rules)
- Links or paths to `.cursor/breakdowns/`, `.cursor/plans/`, or `.cursor/rules/`

**Use instead:**

- In-app navigation paths (**Dashboard → Teams → Edit**, **Settings → Users**, sidebar labels, page titles, buttons, tabs)
- What the operator sees and clicks — not Laravel/Filament/server internals
- Sibling doc links: `[Title](./sibling-page.md)`
- For engineering steps, say to coordinate with engineering or refer to internal breakdowns — do not paste CLI into admin docs

## Member docs (`docs/members/`)

- No "For administrators:" sections or admin-doc cross-references
- Passing mentions OK (e.g. "admins are notified")
- Same bans as admin docs: no `php artisan`, shell blocks, or `.cursor/` references

## After adding a doc

1. Place the file under the correct audience folder (`docs/admin/` or `docs/members/`)
2. Update `docs/README.md` with a link if it helps discovery
3. Keep titles and tone consistent with sibling pages

There is no Docusaurus build step. Preview by reading the markdown locally.

## Git and agents

### Agents must not commit unless asked

- **NEVER** run `git commit` or `git push` for documentation unless the user **explicitly** asks
- Editing markdown does **not** imply permission to commit

### When documentation changes

At the end of work that touched `docs/`, provide a **suggested commit** the user can copy (do not commit unless asked):

```
Summary: <imperative verb> <what changed in docs>

<body — 1–2 sentences on what readers will find updated>
```

If app code and docs both changed, suggest **separate** commit messages (one for code, one for docs) unless the user prefers a single commit.

### When the user asks to commit

Follow the repo's normal git commit rules. Do not use bot/agent author metadata.

## Do not

- Docusaurus sites, `sidebars.ts`, or nested git repos under `docs/`
- Filament navigation examples or ELU-specific paths/URLs
- `ADMIN_DOCS_URL`, `USER_DOCS_URL`, or `config/docs.php` (not used in this project)
- Markdown guides at repo root outside `docs/` (except project README if appropriate)
- `php artisan`, shell deploy blocks, or `.cursor/` references inside `docs/admin/` or `docs/members/`

## Examples

✅ `docs/admin/managing-teams.md` — "Open **Teams** in the sidebar, then **Create team**…"
✅ `docs/members/your-profile.md` — member how-to with no admin cross-links
✅ `.cursor/breakdowns/20260801-1230-teams-admin-breakdown.md` — migrate, test commands, deploy
❌ `docs/managing-teams.md` at the root of `docs/` (use audience subfolders)
❌ `php artisan migrate` inside `docs/admin/managing-teams.md`
